decisions.descriptionMarkdown:
Fast mode lives in `fast/` modules of the crates it touches:

- `crates/gpui/src/fast/`:
  - `mod.rs`, `mode.rs`, `stats.rs`, `verify.rs`;
  - `bounds_tree.rs`, `scene.rs`, `glyphs.rs`, `number_shaping.rs`, `path_cache.rs`;
  - `layout.rs`, `layout_key.rs`, `text.rs`;
  - `dependencies.rs`, `retained.rs`, `splice.rs`, `dispatch.rs`;
  - `composition.rs`, `layers/`, `scenarios/` and `tests/`;
- `fast/layers` and `fast/composition` in `gpui_wgpu`, `gpui_apple`, `gpui_macos`, `gpui_linux`, `gpui_windows` and `gpui_web`.

File names follow gpui-fast, so a later gpui-fast fix can be read beside the gpux file it concerns. Existing gpux files get hooks only: a field typed by a `fast/` struct, a call into `crate::fast::...` written by full path, or a visibility change. Logic and bookkeeping stay in `fast/`. gpui-fast is a read-only reference cloned outside the repository; its code is adapted, never vendored.

Scenarios are `fast::scenarios::*` fixtures in `gpux`, compiled under `bench-support` or `test-support` like `randomized_element_tree`. Each fixture exposes `build`, `step(frame)` and `expect(mode, stats)`, so the bench and the lane-A attribution test share it.

**The bench.** `crates/gpui_platform/benches/fast_mode.rs` runs each fixture per mode through `#[gpux::bench]` and `bench_metrics`. It prints one `gpux-fast-stats: <id> <counter>=<n> ...` line per id.

**The report.** `gpux-testkit` (`tooling/testkit/src/fast_mode.rs`) runs the suite, parses Criterion estimates and stats lines, and renders `fast-mode.md`:
- per-scenario tables;
- deltas against `off` and against the previous mode;
- a per-mechanism ranking;
- `--compare` against an earlier run directory.

Lane G's bench plan adds `fast_mode` to `BENCHES`. The pre-optimization baseline is a saved run directory.

Hot-path redraws notify the owning view instead of calling `Window::refresh()`:

- programmatic scroll and `ScrollActivity` steps notify the scroll owner and its unique dependents through the existing publication path;
- hover, active and group-hover changes notify the innermost view, and `fast::retained` marks that subtree dirty;
- editable-text, text-selection and key-dispatch redraws notify their view.

`refresh()` remains for whole-window changes, each annotated.
